@startuml delivery-state
title Delivery — Canonical V1 Lifecycle
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> PLANNED
PLANNED --> SCHEDULED
SCHEDULED --> DISPATCHED
DISPATCHED --> IN_TRANSIT
IN_TRANSIT --> ATTEMPTED : record attempt
ATTEMPTED --> DELIVERED : complete delivery
ATTEMPTED --> PARTIALLY_DELIVERED : partial outcome
ATTEMPTED --> ATTEMPT_FAILED : failed attempt
ATTEMPT_FAILED --> RESCHEDULED : operations decision
RESCHEDULED --> SCHEDULED : new window
ATTEMPT_FAILED --> FAILED_FINAL : operations exhaustion decision
PLANNED --> CANCELLED
SCHEDULED --> CANCELLED
RESCHEDULED --> CANCELLED

DELIVERED --> [*]
PARTIALLY_DELIVERED --> [*]
CANCELLED --> [*]
FAILED_FINAL --> [*]

note right of ATTEMPTED
Assignment is an active/history fact, not a Delivery state.
Failed attempts remain under this Delivery; no fixed attempt count.
end note

note right of PARTIALLY_DELIVERED
Preserve the immutable outcome and create one
idempotent parent-to-child Continuation Delivery
for remaining obligation.
end note
@enduml
